1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,620
When spam calls come in,
or promotional calls -

2
00:00:03,620 --> 00:00:07,100
any call like that - they
really disturb you, don't they?

3
00:00:07,140 --> 00:00:08,450
So when such a call comes,

4
00:00:08,450 --> 00:00:11,250
your phone itself picks
it up automatically,

5
00:00:11,250 --> 00:00:13,400
asks them why they're calling,

6
00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:15,700
who they're calling for and why -

7
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:18,450
it gets all those details from them,

8
00:00:18,450 --> 00:00:21,150
works out whether it's a call you want,

9
00:00:21,150 --> 00:00:23,200
and rejects the call,

10
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:27,000
or else forwards the call to you.

11
00:00:27,050 --> 00:00:28,770
That's a brilliant AI assistant,

12
00:00:28,770 --> 00:00:30,440
and I'm introducing it in this video.

13
00:00:30,850 --> 00:00:32,880
For more useful videos like this,

14
00:00:32,880 --> 00:00:35,200
subscribe to the channel right now,

15
00:00:35,250 --> 00:00:37,590
and share this video with others

16
00:00:37,590 --> 00:00:39,500
so people know this is possible.

17
00:00:39,620 --> 00:00:42,090
So let's see how it's done.

18
00:00:42,320 --> 00:00:46,100
Welcome, everyone, to
a new V Create video.

19
00:00:46,350 --> 00:00:48,760
For this, we use an app.

20
00:00:48,760 --> 00:00:51,450
It works on iPhone and Android alike.

21
00:00:52,170 --> 00:00:54,500
If you need it, the link is

22
00:00:54,500 --> 00:00:56,480
in the description -
download it from there.

23
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:02,430
Open the app - how to set it up,

24
00:01:02,430 --> 00:01:04,950
the app itself will call you and explain.

25
00:01:05,360 --> 00:01:08,220
So I don't need to explain all of it,

26
00:01:09,020 --> 00:01:11,700
but just to introduce it to you,

27
00:01:12,050 --> 00:01:13,490
I'll open it and show you.

28
00:01:13,910 --> 00:01:16,710
Open the app, enter your phone number,

29
00:01:17,100 --> 00:01:19,360
verify with the OTP and move on.

30
00:01:19,650 --> 00:01:22,450
After that, it gives
you a few instructions.

31
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:27,650
Allow whatever permissions it
needs - contacts, and likewise

32
00:01:27,650 --> 00:01:30,210
the microphone - it asks
for several permissions.

33
00:01:31,100 --> 00:01:33,300
You can allow them without worry.

34
00:01:33,300 --> 00:01:36,710
It works without affecting
your privacy at all -

35
00:01:36,710 --> 00:01:40,570
they promise that when they call you.

36
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:44,530
Then create your full profile.

37
00:01:44,850 --> 00:01:47,400
Once you're in the app,

38
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:49,900
you'll see an option called 'You'.

39
00:01:50,180 --> 00:01:55,120
From there you can switch
it on or off anytime.

40
00:01:55,600 --> 00:01:58,520
Then, to give it the
instructions you need,

41
00:01:59,250 --> 00:02:02,850
select 'Your Instructions'
and set them there.

42
00:02:03,300 --> 00:02:06,260
How should that instruction work?

43
00:02:06,260 --> 00:02:09,520
Busy? The same instruction for every call?

44
00:02:10,700 --> 00:02:13,380
Or only for business calls?

45
00:02:13,380 --> 00:02:16,290
You can choose any of these here.

46
00:02:16,290 --> 00:02:17,700
As you choose each one,

47
00:02:17,700 --> 00:02:20,800
the options it needs are right here -

48
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:23,110
read them and apply what you need.

49
00:02:23,150 --> 00:02:26,110
Then tap 'Add new instruction'

50
00:02:26,110 --> 00:02:29,380
to give it a new instruction by voice,

51
00:02:29,380 --> 00:02:32,480
or create one right here.

52
00:02:33,950 --> 00:02:37,270
Do it that way, or send
a message if you prefer -

53
00:02:37,270 --> 00:02:39,920
whichever you want, select it,

54
00:02:39,920 --> 00:02:42,500
and create your assistant right here.

55
00:02:42,830 --> 00:02:45,990
Also, which calls should
the assistant handle?

56
00:02:45,990 --> 00:02:48,440
Open 'Your Call Preferences',

57
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:52,000
then pick 'All calls'
or 'All calls except',

58
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:55,580
or 'Only unknown numbers'.

59
00:02:55,950 --> 00:02:58,570
If, for unknown numbers,

60
00:02:58,570 --> 00:03:01,300
you want to know who, how and why

61
00:03:01,300 --> 00:03:04,900
before you take the call
- that's the best option.

62
00:03:05,180 --> 00:03:08,550
Select what you need, and tap 'Confirm'.

63
00:03:08,700 --> 00:03:10,800
After that, before you take a call,

64
00:03:10,800 --> 00:03:13,800
the AI assistant talks to them,

65
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:16,980
decides whether you need
the call, and passes it on.

66
00:03:17,300 --> 00:03:20,770
To set the languages it speaks with them,

67
00:03:20,770 --> 00:03:23,660
there's a 'Voice & Language' section.

68
00:03:23,970 --> 00:03:26,540
Select it, and choose
the languages you need

69
00:03:26,540 --> 00:03:29,480
right here - tap 'Edit',

70
00:03:29,950 --> 00:03:32,610
pick the languages you like,

71
00:03:32,610 --> 00:03:36,890
confirm, and those are
the languages it will use.

72
00:03:37,020 --> 00:03:40,140
You can pick three languages at a time.

73
00:03:40,350 --> 00:03:42,590
Confirm, then the primary language

74
00:03:42,590 --> 00:03:45,960
you want can also be chosen here.

75
00:03:46,360 --> 00:03:49,020
Then tap 'Confirm'.

76
00:03:49,350 --> 00:03:51,710
When it first talks to someone,

77
00:03:51,710 --> 00:03:53,750
the language you chose as primary -

78
00:03:53,900 --> 00:03:56,940
it asks the caller
questions in that language.

79
00:03:57,450 --> 00:04:00,310
Whether they speak Malayalam,
Hindi or any other language,

80
00:04:00,310 --> 00:04:03,080
it automatically switches
to that same language,

81
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:06,260
asks questions, gives answers,

82
00:04:06,260 --> 00:04:09,280
and works out exactly
whether you need the call.

83
00:04:09,850 --> 00:04:12,490
This voice that asks the questions -

84
00:04:12,600 --> 00:04:15,020
if you want to change the voice,

85
00:04:15,020 --> 00:04:18,340
select 'Assistant Voice'
at the top, then 'Edit',

86
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:23,060
and pick any voice you like from here.

87
00:04:23,350 --> 00:04:27,590
Select it and confirm, and that's
the voice callers will hear.

88
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:31,250
Likewise, for unknown callers -

89
00:04:31,250 --> 00:04:34,390
should the phone ring,
or switch to silent mode?

90
00:04:34,390 --> 00:04:36,580
You can choose that here.

91
00:04:36,580 --> 00:04:39,500
Promotional calls and the
like can automatically

92
00:04:39,550 --> 00:04:41,910
be set to go silent, all of them.

93
00:04:42,100 --> 00:04:45,240
So many features - a brilliant app.

94
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:48,240
Try it today - the link
is in the description.

95
00:04:48,350 --> 00:04:50,150
If you have any doubts,

96
00:04:50,150 --> 00:04:53,030
you can ask Equal itself, right here -

97
00:04:53,100 --> 00:04:55,380
tap 'Talk to Equal' and ask them,

98
00:04:55,380 --> 00:04:58,140
and they'll clear up
whatever doubts you have.

99
00:04:59,100 --> 00:05:02,640
They'll call you the same
way and explain things.

100
00:05:03,350 --> 00:05:04,550
Very useful, isn't it?

101
00:05:04,550 --> 00:05:08,310
It has free features, and you
can also upgrade for more.

102
00:05:08,400 --> 00:05:12,550
Try what you need first, then decide.

103
00:05:12,600 --> 00:05:15,440
Anyway, I'm sure this
video will be useful.

104
00:05:15,440 --> 00:05:18,100
See you again with more
new things like this.

